<main>

  <!-- STATEMENT -->
  <section class="statement wrap" id="room">
    <div class="statement__grid">
      <div>
        <p class="eyebrow">What it is</p>
        <p class="neg">
          It&rsquo;s not a gallery.<br>
          It&rsquo;s not a retail store.<br>
          It&rsquo;s not a traditional party.
          <span class="is">It&rsquo;s a room for <b>becoming</b>.</span>
        </p>
        <p class="statement__note">
          Each time, a single room in the Arts District holds art, wardrobe, alteration,
          sound, wellness and hospitality at once, and everyone those things belong to. <strong>It opens all ages at noon and returns at five as a 21+ evening</strong>.
          Same room, same making. Different light.
        </p>
      </div>

      <figure class="plate">
        <img src="assets/img/room-tall.jpg" width="1080" height="1350" loading="lazy" decoding="async"
             alt="Brick wall, worktable and stools inside the MAKEROOM space, raking afternoon light across the floor.">
      </figure>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- PROGRAM -->
  <section class="prog wrap" id="program">
    <div class="prog__head">
      <p class="eyebrow">The program</p>
    </div>

    <ul class="prog__list">
      <li class="item">
        <h2 class="item__word">Art</h2>
        <p class="item__gloss">Original work by Kay Wheeler on the brick, and installations that stay live from noon to close.</p>
      </li>
      <li class="item">
        <h2 class="item__word">Fashion</h2>
        <p class="item__gloss">A clothing swap, trade and alteration bar. Bring a piece, take a piece, or rework the one you came in wearing.</p>
      </li>
      <li class="item">
        <h2 class="item__word">Create</h2>
        <p class="item__gloss">A family-style table of prompts, collage, patches and open-ended making. Nothing you make here has to be finished.</p>
      </li>
      <li class="item">
        <h2 class="item__word">Sound</h2>
        <p class="item__gloss">Quiet enough to work through the afternoon. A DJ once the light drops.</p>
      </li>
      <li class="item">
        <h2 class="item__word">Wellness</h2>
        <p class="item__gloss">Youth Dealer - Make Room Wellness: pop-up micro facials and beauty care, plus a guided breathwork session led by a visiting instructor to open the day.</p>
      </li>
      <li class="item">
        <h2 class="item__word">Hospitality</h2>
        <p class="item__gloss">Coffee through the afternoon. Wine, mocktails and food trucks parked outside from five.</p>
      </li>
    </ul>
  </section>

  <!-- EXPERIMENT -->
  <section class="exp">
    <div class="wrap exp__grid">
      <div>
        <p class="eyebrow eyebrow--lit">The experiment</p>
        <h2>The format can change.<em>The invitation stays the same.</em></h2>
      </div>
      <div>
        <p>
          MAKEROOM is built as an experiment, not a template. Every activation recombines
          the same materials: artists, fashion, objects, sound, hospitality, wellness,
          community. Each one becomes a room that has never existed in exactly that
          arrangement before.
        </p>
        <p>
          One month it leans gallery. The next it leans workshop, or listening room, or
          dinner. What stays fixed is the invitation: come as you are, make something,
          take something, leave a little different.
        </p>
        <p>
          There is always room for another idea, another perspective, another version of yourself.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="wrap recombine" role="group" aria-label="The recurring elements of each activation">
      <span>Artists</span><i aria-hidden="true">&times;</i>
      <span>Fashion</span><i aria-hidden="true">&times;</i>
      <span>Objects</span><i aria-hidden="true">&times;</i>
      <span>Sound</span><i aria-hidden="true">&times;</i>
      <span>Hospitality</span><i aria-hidden="true">&times;</i>
      <span>Wellness</span><i aria-hidden="true">&times;</i>
      <span>Community</span>
    </div>

    <p class="vert exp__edge">Arts District &nbsp;&middot;&nbsp; Los Angeles</p>
  </section>

  <!-- COMMUNITY -->
  <section class="people wrap">
    <div class="people__grid">
      <figure class="plate">
        <img src="assets/img/portrait-kay.jpg" width="1080" height="1350" loading="lazy" decoding="async"
             alt="Kay Wheeler, photographed in black and white against a brick wall.">
      </figure>

      <div>
        <p class="eyebrow">Founder</p>

        <div class="bio">
          <h3>Kay Wheeler</h3>
          <p class="bio__role">Featured artist</p>
          <p class="bio__txt">
            A multi-disciplinary artist and stylist working across art, wardrobe and
            hospitality in Los Angeles. The original work on the brick is theirs, made
            for this room. MAKEROOM began with a question they kept asking: what would
            a room look like if nobody in it had to pick one category to be?
          </p>
        </div>

        <div class="bio">
          <<h3 class="bio__logo">
  <a href="https://majesticartgallery.org/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">
    <img src="assets/img/majestic-logo.png" width="560" height="273" loading="lazy">
  </a>
</h3>>
          <p class="bio__role">Community arts partner</p>
          <p class="bio__txt">
            A DTLA 501(c)(3) nonprofit empowering children and families through art and advocacy.
            Majestic anchors the family-facing side of the room and receives all in-kind
            support for the activation.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div class="bio">
          <h3 class="bio__logo bio__logo--tall"><a href="https://youthdealer.myshopify.com/" target="_blank" rel="noopener"><img src="assets/img/youthdealer-logo.png" width="460" height="690" loading="lazy" decoding="async" alt="Youth Dealer"></a></h3>
          <p class="bio__role">Wellness partner</p>
          <p class="bio__txt">
            A skincare line centering melanin and honoring every shade, founded by
            licensed esthetician Brandi J. Andrews on the belief that care should feel
            intentional, not rushed. Youth Dealer runs Make Room Wellness: pop-up micro
            facials, skin consultations and beauty care through the afternoon.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- CLOSE -->
